  "tagline": "Rust-native, Spark Connect-compatible engine for SQL, DataFrame and streaming jobs without the JVM.",
  "description": "Sail, from LakeSail, is a distributed compute engine written in Rust on Apache DataFusion that speaks the Spark Connect protocol, so existing PySpark and Spark SQL code can run against it without rewrites. It starts instantly, runs locally from a pip install or on Kubernetes, and reads and writes Delta Lake and Iceberg on object storage. LakeSail publishes TPC-H and ClickBench results showing large speed and cost gains over JVM Spark. It is an attractive option for cutting Spark infrastructure cost; Spark API coverage is still growing, so check your workloads.",
